{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++0x code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++0x code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <fstream>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <utility>\nusing namespace std;\n\ntypedef long long ll;\ntypedef long double ld;\ntypedef pair<ll, ll> fraction;\n\nint nod(int a, int b) {\n    while (b != 0) {\n        int r = a % b;\n        a = b;\n        b = r;\n    }\n    return a;\n}\n\nfraction reduce_fraction(int x, int y) {\n    int g = nod(x, y);\n    return make_pair((ll)(x / g), (ll)(y / g));\n}\n\nfraction search_best(int x, int y, int n) {\n    ld best = 1000050000.;\n    ld target = (ld)x / y;\n    fraction best_frac;\n\n    for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {\n        ld value = (ld)x * i / y;\n\n        ld low = floorl(value);\n        ld error = std::abs(low / i - target);\n        if (error < best) {\n            best_frac = make_pair((ll)low, (ll)i);\n            best = error;\n        }\n\n        ld high = ceill(value);\n        error = std::abs(high / i - target);\n        if (error < best) {\n            best_frac = make_pair((ll)high, (ll)i);\n            best = error;\n        }\n    }\n\n    return best_frac;\n}\n\nfraction solve(int x, int y, int n) {\n    if (n >= y) return reduce_fraction(x, y);\n    return search_best(x, y, n);\n}\n\nint main() {\n#ifndef ONLINE_JUDGE\n#define cin fin\n    ifstream fin(\"omg.txt\");\n#endif\n    int x, y, n;\n    cin >> x >> y >> n;\n\n    fraction ans = solve(x, y, n);\n\n    cout << ans.first << \"/\" << ans.second << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nimport math\n\ndef nod(a, b):\n    while b != 0:\n        r = a % b\n        a = b\n        b = r\n    return a\n\ndef reduce_fraction(x, y):\n    g = nod(x, y)\n    return (x // g, y // g)\n\ndef search_best(x, y, n):\n    best = 1000050000.0\n    target = x / y\n    best_frac = (0, 1)\n\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        value = x * i / y\n\n        low = math.floor(value)\n        error = abs(low / i - target)\n        if error < best:\n            best_frac = (low, i)\n            best = error\n\n        high = math.ceil(value)\n        error = abs(high / i - target)\n        if error < best:\n            best_frac = (high, i)\n            best = error\n\n    return best_frac\n\ndef solve(x, y, n):\n    if n >= y:\n        return reduce_fraction(x, y)\n    return search_best(x, y, n)\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    x, y, n = map(int, data[:3])\n    ans = solve(x, y, n)\n    print(f\"{ans[0]}/{ans[1]}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.98\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-1.4305104514278355e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -6.007967749610543e-05, -0.0009575072908774018, -0.10020658373832703, -0.0019838192965835333, -0.0019288521725684404, 0.0, -0.029783163219690323, -0.0002985746832564473, -0.693649411201477, -2.3841830625315197e-06, -0.04860583692789078, 0.0, -0.0007127366843633354, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.11645442992448807, 0.0, -0.00247577065